course: dictionary
lesson: 5397
title: Kongo: a people, a kingdom and a language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Kongo is one word with three jobs, and the clues around it tell you which job it does. It can name a people of Central Africa, a kingdom, or a language. Ask yourself: is the sentence about people, a place ruled by a king, or words someone speaks?
explain: «In 1526 King Afonso I of Kongo wrote to the king of Portugal complaining about it.» The words King and kingdom tell you that Kongo here is a kingdom, a land ruled by a king. Read the words around the word and let them point you to the right meaning.
explain: «In Europa Universalis 5 you can see Mali, Ethiopia, Kongo and Kilwa in 1337.» Kongo sits in a list of places with Mali, Ethiopia and Kilwa, so here it names a place. Europa Universalis 5 is a game, so this sentence shows you the word on a map of the past.
fact: Kongo is a noun. It can name a people, a kingdom or a language.
fact: The Kongo people live in Angola, the Republic of the Congo and the Democratic Republic of the Congo.
fact: The Kingdom of Kongo was a large African kingdom on the Atlantic coast from about 1390 to the 1800s.
fact: Kongo (Kikongo) is the language of the Kongo people.
fact: The Congo River and the countries named Congo take their name from the Kongo.
exercise: «In 1526 King Afonso I of Kongo wrote to the king of Portugal.» In this sentence, what is Kongo? | A type of food | A language spoken in Portugal | A river in Africa | *A kingdom, ruled by a king
exercise: What is Kikongo? | *The language of the Kongo people | A kind of Kongo art | A slang word for average | A mountain in Angola
exercise: Which country is one where the Kongo people live? | Japan | Brazil | Canada | *Angola
test: «King Afonso I of Kongo» shows Kongo as which of these? | A river | A person's name | A language | *A kingdom
test: In «Kongo art», what does the word Kongo describe? | The language | *The art | The river | The people only
exam: Jayden reads «The Kingdom of Kongo was a large African kingdom on the Atlantic coast from about 1390 to the 1800s.» What does Kongo name here? | A people | *A kingdom | A river | A language
